{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1168746-levels-of-directness-in-acts-of-hubris","id":1168746,"title":"Levels of directness in Acts of Hubris","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-19T02:21:29-08:00","id":1168746,"title":"Levels of directness in Acts of Hubris","content":"I recently played as a Moros of the Thread-Cutter Legacy (mystical assassins using Death and Fate), a legacy I think is a lot of fun to explore. In the session I had a mission to kill off a mid-level drug dealer and it ended up as a small massacre with him and 3-4 of his gangster bodyguards. My character however did not kill anyone, he did not even hurt anyone. He simply used Fate to &quot;summon&quot; a 3 dot Retainer, an ex-military who had vowed to avenge the death by overdose of his sister. I then persuaded him that we had the same goals and guided him into the right building and used Fate again to boost his skills as he went through all the bodyguards and then the drug dealer himself.<br /> <br /> This got us thinking if I would have to roll Wisdom or not. Premeditaded murder and violence is an example of an Act of Hubris at Wisdom 7, but since I did kill someone with magic but in a rather indirect fashion we were not sure if I would have to roll for degeneration or not. Also, I did not expose the sleeper retainer to obvious magic, only subtle Fate spells. What would you say?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T03:01:32-08:00","id":1168748,"title":"","content":"You cast spells with the overt intent of achieving the end of making a man die; it's not like you befriended this dude in unrelated circumstances and then buffed him with magic because you didn't want to see <i>him</i> die. Eat that Wisdom check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T03:56:43-08:00","id":1168754,"title":"","content":"It's definitely a Wisdom violation because of the intent of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T04:46:09-08:00","id":1168768,"title":"","content":"Yeah clearly an act of hubris. Not only is the intent to get someone killed, your PC is also responsible for a small massacre. This would have been an act of hubris even without magic involved, you know. <br /> The escalation of violence beyond the premeditated murder would probable be worth a lower Wisdom breaking point but the scale is so broad as it falls in the Understanding rating, 4-7.<br /> Wisdom goes hand in hand with ethical thinking and in game, different views on ethics is one of the reasons mage is a really epic game, but off-game it's a clear violation of Wisdom.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T05:31:31-08:00","id":1168775,"title":"","content":"THank you for your answers! This is not me trying to worm away from a Wisdom roll, this is me wanting to understand better the principles behind Acts of Hubris.<br /> <br /> I was not sure about whether magic needs to be involved or not for it to be an Act of Hubris, but if you say it is then I will follow that logic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T06:37:22-08:00","id":1168789,"title":"","content":"I agree with these guys. I would put it at 3 dice. If the massacre were intended I'd probably put it at 1 die, but since it was an unintended consequence I would let it slide and leave the Wisdom roll at 3 dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T08:57:21-08:00","id":1168811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1168746-levels-of-directness-in-acts-of-hubris?p=1168775#post1168775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THank you for your answers! This is not me trying to worm away from a Wisdom roll, this is me wanting to understand better the principles behind Acts of Hubris.<br /> <br /> I was not sure about whether magic needs to be involved or not for it to be an Act of Hubris, but if you say it is then I will follow that logic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wisdom is explicitly not tied directly to morality like it was in previous editions. However, some of it is still bound up in morality, and for good reason. You will notice than many lesser crimes are not considered Wisdom violations, and if you inure yourself to a spell you will never have a Wisdom violation when using that spell, no matter what you do with it.<br /> <br /> The idea behind Wisdom and Acts of Hubris in second edition is about how far will your character go when it comes to ends justifying the means. This is why you get Rampant or Megalomaniacal when you fail a Wisdom degeneration roll. Mage is not a game that asks &quot;can you do it?&quot; Instead, it's a game that asks &quot;should you do it?&quot; Mages can do basically anything (especially at 4 or 5 dots, to say nothing of archmastery). But is the shortcut always the right path?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T10:50:04-08:00","id":1168849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1168746-levels-of-directness-in-acts-of-hubris?p=1168789#post1168789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with these guys. I would put it at 3 dice. If the massacre were intended I'd probably put it at 1 die, but since it was an unintended consequence I would let it slide and leave the Wisdom roll at 3 dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is, it seems to me, the exact WRONG way of handling it. Premediated murder is at 3 dice, while murdering in a rage is at 1 die. WIsdom is about being in control of yourself and the consequences of your actions. Unintended consequences make a wisdom roll worse, not better for you. If you kill someone accidentially it should be a falling act, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> That said (and now we get a bit into homebrew) I'd allow a mage of the Thread Cutter legacy to kill people that need to die without a wisdom roll. He shaped his soul into a tool of bringing the right end at the right time, doing so will not weaken the integrity of his soul. Doesn't mean all murder should be sacroscant, only those that happen in direct pursuit of his legacies philosophy. Speaking of which I think the dead bodyguards would not be in line with his philosophy and were (probably?) unintended consequences. I'd place this as a falling act of wisdom, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T12:04:54-08:00","id":1168875,"title":"","content":"You've convinced me. He should have controlled the situation better. 1 die for the unintended deaths, and I would still say 1 die for intended deaths as well given that it really isn't his philosophy to kill the bodyguards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T12:18:35-08:00","id":1168882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1168746-levels-of-directness-in-acts-of-hubris?p=1168849#post1168849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That said (and now we get a bit into homebrew) I'd allow a mage of the Thread Cutter legacy to kill people that need to die without a wisdom roll. He shaped his soul into a tool of bringing the right end at the right time, doing so will not weaken the integrity of his soul. Doesn't mean all murder should be sacroscant, only those that happen in direct pursuit of his legacies philosophy. Speaking of which I think the dead bodyguards would not be in line with his philosophy and were (probably?) unintended consequences. I'd place this as a falling act of wisdom, really.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You can't protect yourself from hubris by changing the soul-container to better be able to use hubristic actions. There is however a point to be made about acting in accordance with your Virtue as in the reasoning &quot;The character may very well understand and see the consequences of her actions, but she stands by them because she truly, fundamentally believes her actions are righteous&quot;. However the Thread Cutter would probably not have above average Wisdom scores, because they believe it's their right to end peoples lives for a greater good. However I think it's probably very common in that Legacy to Inure a particular spell and use that to to the &quot;thread cutting&quot;. This is a hubristic action, it hurt's the soul and invites the Abyss, but many mages believes it for a greater good. <br /> <br /> Just giving the Legacy the ability to kill without consequence to their Wisdom seems pretty short cut for interesting drama as well as ethical problems. <br /> This however brings up the Masques and the Roles that the Guardians have perfected to the level of playing a Role and use that Role to take on the burden of Wisdom loss/hubristic acts.<br /> This brings up some really metaphysical interesting points about Identity, sociology and Role Theory and what and how it's implemented in the cosmology of CofD. Shadow name, Occulation and Astral dream form is of course other points that cements that identity has a larger impact on the metaphysical realm then we'd normally would presume. <br /> <br /> So if not assuming that every member is a high Masque merit spy in the Veil, one should perhaps look at their Attainment and see if anything could be done with their Wisdom loss potential, although it's not really higher then many other Legacies that are in clear day-by-day violation of the Understanding Wisdom level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T12:40:03-08:00","id":1168886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1168746-levels-of-directness-in-acts-of-hubris?p=1168882#post1168882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't protect yourself from hubris by changing the soul-container to better be able to use hubristic actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can to some extent, that's the entire point of legacy attainments and inuring spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T12:49:27-08:00","id":1168889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1168746-levels-of-directness-in-acts-of-hubris?p=1168886#post1168886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can to some extent, that's the entire point of legacy attainments and inuring spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Legacy Attainments are excempt from Wisdom loss. My (as I pointed out homebrew) approach merely extends this to the whole legacy philosophy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T13:41:31-08:00","id":1168907,"title":"","content":"Wisdom in Mage is pretty flexible. First, the book says that the list they give is just a set of examples, it's one of the places that can experience heavy editing by the ST. Second, there are multiple ways of undermining those examples through the mechanics of Mage via the player's choices. Mages suffer Wisdom loss primarily through impulsive action that creates unintended consequences, but over the course of their development, Mages get to decide what's Wise and what isn't. This may lead to giving the Abyss an advantage in attempting to influence their magic, but in the end, it's a Mage who by him or herself who determines what's Wisdom. The flexibility of Wisdom is why no one Order or Legacy has ever been acknowledged as Wise above all the others, including the Scelesti, Banishers and the Seers. No one has a monopoly on Wisdom, except the Mage who has Obsessed over Wisdom and how to obtain it, and even their beliefs are undercut by the Mage who is diametrically opposed, but no less dedicated to finding the truth of Wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T15:44:57-08:00","id":1168937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1168746-levels-of-directness-in-acts-of-hubris?p=1168886#post1168886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can to some extent, that's the entire point of legacy attainments and inuring spells.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah you're totally correct. Forgot that Attainments are not considered an act of hubris whatever it is or what you do with it, like Inured spells.<br /> One could argue about that instead but it is what it is. So i take back some of my arguments at least ^_^<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T02:55:34-08:00","id":1169039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1168746-levels-of-directness-in-acts-of-hubris?p=1168889#post1168889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. Legacy Attainments are excempt from Wisdom loss. My (as I pointed out homebrew) approach merely extends this to the whole legacy philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I agree with this. Legacies are an expression of how the mage <i>knows</i> the world should be - knows so thoroughly that they remake themselves on the most fundamental level. So I agree with putting the Thread-Cutter off the hook for the drug dealer but on it for the collateral massacre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T04:12:10-08:00","id":1169045,"title":"","content":"So Tremere and other soul eating Reaper Legacies don't get any wisdom loss if they try to live longer by self-mutilating necromancy and eating peoples souls, even without attainments. Seems pretty counter to what Wisdom's about and the whole &quot;should we do it&quot; as well as the hubristic theme of the game.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T04:48:12-08:00","id":1169051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1168746-levels-of-directness-in-acts-of-hubris?p=1169045#post1169045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Tremere and other soul eating Reaper Legacies don't get any wisdom loss if they try to live longer by self-mutilating necromancy and eating peoples souls, even without attainments. Seems pretty counter to what Wisdom's about and the whole &amp;quot;should we do it&amp;quot; as well as the hubristic theme of the game.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It does fit with the fact that there -isn\u2019t- a universal form of Wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T05:10:06-08:00","id":1169052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1168746-levels-of-directness-in-acts-of-hubris?p=1169045#post1169045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Tremere and other soul eating Reaper Legacies don't get any wisdom loss if they try to live longer by self-mutilating necromancy and eating peoples souls, even without attainments. Seems pretty counter to what Wisdom's about and the whole &amp;quot;should we do it&amp;quot; as well as the hubristic theme of the game.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, nobody said being Wise meant being good...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T07:53:19-08:00","id":1169090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1168746-levels-of-directness-in-acts-of-hubris?p=1169045#post1169045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Tremere and other soul eating Reaper Legacies don't get any wisdom loss if they try to live longer by self-mutilating necromancy and eating peoples souls, even without attainments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a) the Tremere aren't just a Legacy anymore and their Legacy equivalents come with attendant Self-Mutilating Necromancy Trade-Offs, b) this is only true for Legacies if you've devoted your magical nature to being a thing fueled by the consumption of souls at the opportunity cost of less ruinous identifiers, and c) the most distant/least fundamental change you can work upon yourself in this vein is still &quot;let a bit of your magic off the leash for the sake of plausible deniability and extra upkeep.&quot;<br /> <br /> The lesson here is that you go big or go home if you want to avoid the immediate long-term consequences of hubris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T09:06:09-08:00","id":1169104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1168746-levels-of-directness-in-acts-of-hubris?p=1169051#post1169051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does fit with the fact that there -isn\u2019t- a universal form of Wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That might be true in real life, but mages have a universal meta-Wisdom. In game there's discussion about the rights'n'wrongs but there still exists a Wisdom trait, which is what is the concern here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1168746-levels-of-directness-in-acts-of-hubris?p=1169052#post1169052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, nobody said being Wise meant being good...</div> </div> </div> </div>No, neither did I. Good and Evil is subjective. However soul eating is bad for your Wisdom. Wisdom != Goodness","signature":"","edited":{"userid":523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","user":"Poseur","date":". 12-20-2017, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T09:19:22-08:00","id":1169106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1168746-levels-of-directness-in-acts-of-hubris?p=1169104#post1169104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That might be true in real life, but mages have a universal meta-Wisdom. In game there's discussion about the rights'n'wrongs but there still exists a Wisdom trait, which is what is the concern here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't inuring, Legacy attainments, etc kind of demonstrate that it is not, in fact, universal?<br /> <br /> In fact, one of the very first things in the 'Losing Wisdom' section is:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M2E P87</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every mage and every circumstance is different from a Wisdom standpoint. Two mages in nearly identical circumstances may cast the same spell or commit the same action, but to one, his Wisdom is safe while the other risks degeneration.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T09:29:07-08:00","id":1169109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1168746-levels-of-directness-in-acts-of-hubris?p=1169090#post1169090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, a) the Tremere aren't just a Legacy anymore and their Legacy equivalents come with attendant Self-Mutilating Necromancy Trade-Offs, b) this is only true for Legacies if you've devoted your magical nature to being a thing fueled by the consumption of souls at the opportunity cost of less ruinous identifiers, and c) the most distant/least fundamental change you can work upon yourself in this vein is still &quot;let a bit of your magic off the leash for the sake of plausible deniability and extra upkeep.&quot;<br /> <br /> The lesson here is that you go big or go home if you want to avoid the immediate long-term consequences of hubris.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well Tremere to the side then if they aren't a Legecy no more. But other Legacies still that have philosophies that are in clear contrast against Wisdom still exist and I still believe it weakens the setting to allow their actions not to suffer Hubris if they are made with the intent of their own philosophy. Want to enslave people without Wisdom loss? Join a Legacy! Want to consume the souls of the Awekened without Wisdom loss? Join a Legacy! Want to summon a few Anunaki without Wisdom loss? Join a Legacy! Want to commit genocide and fuel you spells with really powerful yantras for whatever reason without Wisdom loss? Join a Legacy! Want to unsafely relinquish magic all over the place and try to force sleepers to awaken with it without Wisdom loss? Join a Legacy!<br /> <br /> This, as it might however is a good reason that Mages are Monsters, but it's a cheap reason, paying the cost of what hubris is meant and why Wisdom would be important to the setting. <br /> It's a free from all if it align with legacy philosophy instead of any real drawback or cost outside the social reality. <br /> Inuring spells to avoid hubris comes with the cost of somewhat damaging the soul and opening a small way for the abyss to more easily enter through your magic.<br /> Attainments suffer the same reasoning as this Legacy freedom from hubris, and frankly there's no reason except RAW that attainments should be free from Acts of Hubris, if anyone has a good argument I'm all ears. Why would an action, magical or not, be free from the possibility it could be an Act of Hubris. Example why is it that drowning a man (spell) is an Act, drowning a man (physical action) is an Act but drowning a man (Attainment) is not an Act?<br /> <br /> Either way, at the very least should it be an Act of Hubris to strive to join one of these Legacies that have philosophies that are in clear violation toward Wisdom, the intent is clear that your own intent <i>is </i> to use magic in a very hubristic and cavalier way and you're working towards it, before your soul container could protect your Wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T09:30:14-08:00","id":1169110,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1168746-levels-of-directness-in-acts-of-hubris?p=1169052#post1169052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, nobody said being Wise meant being good...</div> </div> </div> </div>No, neither did I. Good and Evil is subjective. However soul eating is bad for your Wisdom. Wisdom != Goodness","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T09:46:18-08:00","id":1169113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1168746-levels-of-directness-in-acts-of-hubris?p=1169106#post1169106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't inuring, Legacy attainments, etc kind of demonstrate that it is not, in fact, universal?<br /> <br /> In fact, one of the very first things in the 'Losing Wisdom' section is: <i>Originally posted by <b>M2E P87</b></i><br /> <i>Every mage and every circumstance is different from a Wisdom standpoint. Two mages in nearly identical circumstances may cast the same spell or commit the same action, but to one, his Wisdom is safe while the other risks degeneration.</i><br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking, no it's not universal, it's relativistic, based on a plethora of circumstance, but with a few universally applicable things that could be circumvented.<br /> It only demonstrates that mages are good at cheating, even on that. Inuring breaks a part of your soul and makes a crack in the Path you're on to take home supernal truths to the fallen worlds that have an easier time inviting the abyss, which is the cost of ignoring the universal Wisdom, that itself is pretty hubristic. <br /> <br /> The quote from the corebook could just as easily be talking about two mages with different levels of Wisdom or that the spell cast has a different intent, which is more likely then that two mages have a different worldview and therefore ones Wisdom doesn't check for degeneration while the other does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T09:49:06-08:00","id":1169116,"title":"","content":"Just about the only thing universal about Wisdom is that it exists.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if there is a Supernal form of Wisdom then like all of the rest of reality as it filters away from the Supernal it fractures and warps. There are many different kinds of chairs because the ideal, Supernal chair goes through an imperfect interpretive process as it enters the Fallen. The same would happen with Wisdom, and on top of that Mages know how to warp that imperfect interpretation of Wisdom further via Inuring and legacies and so on. This happens on top of the already natural warping that occurs allowing an action to be Hubris for one Mage but not another in similar circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T09:51:39-08:00","id":1169117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1168746-levels-of-directness-in-acts-of-hubris?p=1169109#post1169109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But other Legacies still that have philosophies that are in clear contrast against Wisdom still exist and I still believe it weakens the setting to allow their actions not to suffer Hubris if they are made with the intent of their own philosophy. Want to enslave people without Wisdom loss? Join a Legacy! Want to consume the souls of the Awekened without Wisdom loss? Join a Legacy! Want to summon a few Anunaki without Wisdom loss? Join a Legacy! Want to commit genocide and fuel you spells with really powerful yantras for whatever reason without Wisdom loss? Join a Legacy! Want to unsafely relinquish magic all over the place and try to force sleepers to awaken with it without Wisdom loss? Join a Legacy!</div> </div> </div> </div>Again: This isn't a fucking social club you're talking about, it's <i>reshaping the place where your soul fits in</i>, and you retain your Wisdom <i>when using the magic powers you got from <b>reshaping the place where your soul fits in.</b></i> You have <i>redefined the thing that you are</i> such that the boundary that breaks the containment of your magic no longer lies across this particular threshold. &quot;Join a Legacy&quot; as a solution is like saying &quot;dedicate yourself to a cult.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would an action, magical or not, be free from the possibility it could be an Act of Hubris. Example why is it that drowning a man (spell) is an Act, drowning a man (physical action) is an Act but drowning a man (Attainment) is not an Act? </div> </div> </div>Because by joining a Legacy whose Attainments can drown people you have made drowning people something within the bounds of your your magical identity that you need no special effort to contain or repair in terms of your Nimbus spreading where you don't want it to. The spell has the capacity for the same failsafe with the tradeoff of always having some chance of running wild.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Either way, at the very least should it be an Act of Hubris to strive to join one of these Legacies that have philosophies that are in clear violation toward Wisdom, the intent is clear that your own intent <i>is </i> to use magic in a very hubristic and cavalier way and you're working towards it, before your soul container could protect your Wisdom. </div> </div> </div>The abstract behavior of &quot;striving to shape your soul to hold your magic better&quot; is not an Act of Hubris any more than the behavior of planning to murder someone is. Initiations might veer into actions that shake your Wisdom, as might the nonmagical activities of such a group, but &quot;I wish I could do these things even though it's kind of a bad idea in the long run&quot; is not something that outright damages your ability to confine your Nimbus along your sympathies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T11:38:45-08:00","id":1169155,"title":"","content":"Legacy attainments aren't accessed via the Supernal, so there's no reaching past the Abyss or any of that. They're accessed from your own soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T13:40:32-08:00","id":1169193,"title":"","content":"Wise mages aren\u2019t the ones who ask \u201cDoes this minimize the damage I cause to the world around me?\u201d They\u2019re the ones who ask \u201cCan I handle this?\u201d Minimizing the damage they do to the world is the effect, not purpose, of Wisdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  adding for detail 12-20-2017, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T20:56:25-08:00","id":1169266,"title":"","content":"As much as I go back and forth on the implementation of Wisdom in 2e, I think I'm ok with joining a Legacy inuring you to certain Acts of Hubris.<br /> <br /> The main reason is that you are usually only getting inured to a small subset of potential Widsom violations.<br /> <br /> The example given earlier is a pretty good example of a situation where the PC thought he was being clever in joining the Thread Cutters so that he could engineer the death of the drug dealer, but the ST was more clever in having the situation go sour in such a way that the PC would potential lose Wisdom anyway.<br /> <br /> In practice, in the game, if one of my PCs joins a Legacy to get around one aspect of Hubris, then the themes of the game DEMAND that I introduce complications that put his Wisdom at risk in some other way.<br /> <br /> TLDR: You can't inure yourself to everything. Legacies will only get you so far in this regard. And as Satchel stated: It's reshaping your soul container. Not something to be taken lightly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T05:47:50-08:00","id":1169320,"title":"","content":"While it's true one of the areas of the game is the maintenance of Wisdom, and there's nothing wrong with the ST throwing Wisdom risking complications at their players, there's nothing in the game that demands it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T06:55:10-08:00","id":1169335,"title":"","content":"And since one of the points of joining a Legacy is removing Acts of Hubris the player might expect at least some form of protection. I'm not saying it'd be wrong to have this particular example lead to an AoH roll, but trying to find such loopholes every single time, or even most of the time, is definitely working against that aspect of Legacies.<br /> When it comes to mundane AoHs I'd also let the mage's Legacy inform what level of Wisdom might be most fitting for the AoH. It might be more fitting to have murder by sniper rifle be an AoH on Enlightened instead of Understanding for someone belonging to an assassin legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T08:47:39-08:00","id":1169367,"title":"","content":"There has come up a fair bit of good arguments in this discussion.I think I've reevaluated the situation about the Legacies and such and I'm inclined to agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> et. at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T10:03:30-08:00","id":1169394,"title":"","content":"Building off what I said yesterday about if there is a Supernal ideal of Wisdom, it\u2019s interesting that Wisdom doesn\u2019t fall under the purview of any arcana and is thus immune to direct manipulation via magic unless you employ the powers of beings from the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T14:25:11-08:00","id":1169473,"title":"","content":"To be pedantic about it, Morality traits (such as Wisdom) can be modified through Death 7. However, since it requires Archmastery, it's an academic distinction for most Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T15:53:34-08:00","id":1169759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1168746-levels-of-directness-in-acts-of-hubris?p=1169473#post1169473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be pedantic about it, Morality traits (such as Wisdom) can be modified through Death 7. However, since it requires Archmastery, it's an academic distinction for most Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is, of course, absolutely no indication that this is true in 2E, due to the general change of magical structure, practices, and purviews. Some things that used to require archmastery no longer do (and I can think of at least one that's now doable at 1 dot with some effort).<br /> <br /> It's the best information we have, though, and it serves as an indication that it might be possible, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T04:10:04-08:00","id":1169877,"title":"","content":"I admit, it's a reasonable objection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}